-- title:
--   Ordinarity of the ε-part of every level of the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $O$ be a commutative ring equipped with an algebra structure on $\mathbb{Z}/p$, and let $H$ be a $p$-divisible group of height $h$ over $O$ in the sense of the project structure: a family of commutative rings $H.\mathrm{level}\,v$, each a cocommutative $O$-Hopf algebra that is finite and free as an $O$-module, with surjective bialgebra transition maps $H.\mathrm{level}(v+1)\to H.\mathrm{level}\,v$ of rank $p^{vh}$ at level $v$ and with kernel the ideal $\mathrm{torsionIdeal}$ generated by the image of the augmentation ideal under multiplication by $p^{v}$. Let $u,\varepsilon,w$ be families of $O$-bialgebra endomorphisms of the levels ($\rightarrow_{ac}$ denotes bialgebra homomorphisms) such that: $u$, $\varepsilon$ and $w$ commute with the transition maps; each $\varepsilon_v$ is idempotent; $\varepsilon_v$ commutes with $u_v$; $\varepsilon_v\circ w_v=w_v=w_v\circ\varepsilon_v$; and $w_v$ is a two-sided inverse of $u_v\circ\varepsilon_v$ in the sense $w_v\circ(u_v\circ\varepsilon_v)=\varepsilon_v=(u_v\circ\varepsilon_v)\circ w_v$. Assume furthermore the hypothesis `hFV`: for every bialgebra endomorphism $F_k$ of the special fibre $\mathbb{Z}/p\otimes_O H.\mathrm{level}\,1$ given by $x\mapsto x^{p}$ and every algebra endomorphism $F_D$ of its Cartier dual (the $\mathbb{Z}/p$-linear dual with its convolution ring structure) given by $\psi\mapsto\psi^{p}$, there are an $n\in\mathbb{N}$ and bialgebra endomorphisms $a,b$ of the Cartier dual such that the $n$-th composition power of $\mathrm{CartierDual.map}(\mathrm{id}\otimes u_1)$ equals the convolution product of $F_D\circ a$ and $b\circ\mathrm{CartierDual.map}\,F_k$. The conclusion: for every level $v$, every commutative ring $C_v$ that is a cocommutative $\mathbb{Z}/p$-Hopf algebra, finite and free as a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-module, and every pair of bialgebra maps $q:\mathbb{Z}/p\otimes_O H.\mathrm{level}\,v\to C_v$, $i:C_v\to\mathbb{Z}/p\otimes_O H.\mathrm{level}\,v$ with $q$ surjective, $q\circ i=\mathrm{id}_{C_v}$ and $i\circ q=\mathrm{id}_{\mathbb{Z}/p}\otimes\varepsilon_v$, there exist a commutative ring $M$ that is a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-Hopf algebra, finite and free over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, a commutative ring $E$ that is a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-Hopf algebra, and a bijective bialgebra homomorphism $\Theta:C_v\to M\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p}E$ such that $E$ is reduced and the Cartier dual of $M$ is reduced.
--
--   This is the statement that, under the slope hypothesis `hFV` on the Cartier transpose of the reduced level-one endomorphism $u_1$, the $\varepsilon$-part of the special fibre of the $p$-divisible group is ordinary at every level: any splitting of the idempotent $\mathrm{id}\otimes\varepsilon_v$ decomposes as a tensor product of a group scheme with reduced Cartier dual (multiplicative type) and a reduced one (étale type), with no local–local factor. It feeds the construction of points of the étale part used in [`PDivisibleGroup.exists_point_toAlgHom_eq_comp_of_etale_cartierDual_of_forall_comp_eq_of_reduction_pow_eq_frobenius_conv_verschiebung`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.exists_point_toAlgHom_eq_comp_of_etale_cartierDual_of_forall_comp_eq_of_reduction_pow_eq_frobenius_conv_verschiebung).
